{"task_id": "HumanEval/9", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef rolling_max(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the rolling maximum for a list of integers.\n    The output list contains the maximum value encountered up to each point in the input sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    \n    # Check if all elements are integers. This uses a generator expression for efficiency.\n    if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in numbers):\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements in the 'numbers' list must be integers.\")\n\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    # Initialize with negative infinity to correctly handle lists containing only negative numbers.\n    current_max = float('-inf') \n    for num in numbers:\n        current_max = max(current_max, num)\n        result.append(current_max)\n    return result"}
