{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "class TripletFinder:\n    @staticmethod\n    def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if three distinct elements in the list sum to zero.\n        Raises TypeError or ValueError for invalid input.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(l, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'l' must be a list.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in l):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in 'l' must be integers.\")\n\n        n = len(l)\n        if n < 3:\n            return False\n\n        # Sort the list to efficiently find triplets using a two-pointer approach.\n        l.sort()\n\n        for i in range(n - 2):\n            # Skip duplicate elements for 'i' to avoid processing redundant triplets.\n            if i > 0 and l[i] == l[i - 1]:\n                continue\n\n            left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n            while left < right:\n                current_sum = l[i] + l[left] + l[right]\n                if current_sum == 0:\n                    return True\n                elif current_sum < 0:\n                    left += 1\n                else:  # current_sum > 0\n                    right -= 1\n        return False"}
