{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "class EmptyListError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the input list is empty.\n    Custom exception for empty input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"Input list cannot be empty.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\nclass NonNumericInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the input list contains non-numeric elements.\n    Custom exception for invalid element types.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"Input list must contain only numeric elements (int or float).\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Handles empty and non-numeric inputs with custom exceptions.\"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise EmptyListError()\n\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise NonNumericInputError()\n\n    sorted_data = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_data)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_data[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_data[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_data[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2"}
