{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "import math\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the largest prime factor of n. Assumes n > 1 and is not prime for efficiency.\"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n    d = 2\n\n    # Handle factor 2 explicitly to optimize for even numbers.\n    while n % d == 0:\n        largest_factor = d\n        n //= d\n\n    # Iterate for odd factors up to the square root of the remaining n.\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            largest_factor = d\n            n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor itself.\n    if n > 1:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor"}
