{"task_id": "HumanEval/82", "solution": "import math\ndef _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a prime number.\n    It performs trial division up to the square root of n.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\ndef prime_length(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Returns True if the string length is a prime number or False otherwise.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    length = len(s)\n    return _is_prime(length)"}
