{"task_id": "HumanEval/85", "solution": "class Calculator:\n    def add(self, lst: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of even elements located at odd indices in a list.\n        Raises TypeError for invalid input types or ValueError for an empty list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(lst, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        if not lst:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n        total_sum = 0\n        for i, num in enumerate(lst):\n            if not isinstance(num, int):\n                raise TypeError(f\"List elements must be integers, but found {type(num)} at index {i}.\")\n            if i % 2 != 0 and num % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += num\n        return total_sum"}
