{"task_id": "HumanEval/97", "solution": "class UnitDigitExtractor:\n    def extract(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Extracts the unit digit of an integer. Handles both positive and negative numbers.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n        return abs(n) % 10\n\nclass CalculatorService:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._unit_digit_extractor = UnitDigitExtractor()\n\n    def multiply(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the product of the unit digits of two integers. Raises TypeError if inputs are not integers.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(a, int) or not isinstance(b, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be integers.\")\n\n        unit_digit_a = self._unit_digit_extractor.extract(a)\n        unit_digit_b = self._unit_digit_extractor.extract(b)\n\n        return unit_digit_a * unit_digit_b"}
