{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "# src/pile_generator.py\nclass PileGenerator:\n    \"\"\"\n    A class to generate stone pile levels based on a given integer n.\n    The first level has n stones, and subsequent levels add 2 stones.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def make_a_pile(n: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates and returns a list of stone counts for n levels.\n        Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n        pile = []\n        current_stones = n\n        for _ in range(n):\n            pile.append(current_stones)\n            current_stones += 2\n        return pile"}
