{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "def choose_num(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function takes two integers x and y and returns the biggest even\n    integer in the inclusive range [x, y]. If no such number exists, -1 is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x > y:\n        return -1\n\n    # Iterate downwards from y to x to find the biggest even number first.\n    for num in range(y, x - 1, -1):\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return num\n\n    return -1"}
