{"task_id": "HumanEval/111", "solution": "from collections import Counter\nfrom typing import Dict\nclass HistogramAnalyzer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Analyzes a string of letters to find the most frequent ones.\n    This class encapsulates the core logic for histogram calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def calculate_histogram(self, input_string: str) -> Dict[str, int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes the input string to find the letter(s) with the highest frequency and their counts.\n        Returns an empty dictionary if the input string is empty or contains only spaces.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not input_string:\n            return {}\n\n        letters = input_string.split(' ')\n        # Filter out any empty strings that may result from multiple spaces (e.g., 'a  b' or '   ')\n        letters = [letter for letter in letters if letter]\n\n        if not letters:  # If input was only spaces or became empty after filtering\n            return {}\n\n        counts = Counter(letters)\n        \n        # Determine the maximum count. If counts is empty, max_count remains 0.\n        max_count = max(counts.values()) if counts else 0\n\n        result = {\n            letter: count\n            for letter, count in counts.items()\n            if count == max_count\n        }\n        return result\ndef histogram(test: str) -> Dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    The main entry point for users to calculate the histogram of most frequent letters.\n    It delegates the actual work to the HistogramAnalyzer class.\n    \"\"\"\n    analyzer = HistogramAnalyzer()\n    return analyzer.calculate_histogram(test)"}
