{"task_id": "HumanEval/123", "solution": "class CollatzCalculator:\n    def _generate_sequence(self, n: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Generates the complete Collatz sequence for a given positive integer n.\n        Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n        \n        sequence = [n]\n        current = n\n        while current != 1:\n            if current % 2 == 0:\n                current //= 2\n            else:\n                current = (3 * current) + 1\n            sequence.append(current)\n        return sequence\n\n    def _filter_and_sort_odd(self, sequence: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Filters a sequence to extract unique odd numbers and returns them in sorted order.\"\"\"\n        odd_numbers = sorted(list(set(num for num in sequence if num % 2 != 0)))\n        return odd_numbers\n\n    def get_odd_collatz(self, n: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the Collatz sequence for 'n' and returns a sorted list of unique odd numbers found within it.\n        Propagates ValueError from _generate_sequence for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n        sequence = self._generate_sequence(n)\n        return self._filter_and_sort_odd(sequence)"}
