{"task_id": "HumanEval/156", "solution": "from .constants import ROMAN_MAP\nclass RomanConverter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the RomanConverter instance with the Roman numeral mapping.\"\"\"\n        self._roman_map = ROMAN_MAP\n\n    def convert(self, num: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts an integer into its Roman numeral string equivalent.\n        This method assumes the input number is valid.\n        \"\"\"\n        result = []\n        temp_num = num\n        for value, symbol in self._roman_map:\n            while temp_num >= value:\n                result.append(symbol)\n                temp_num -= value\n        return \"\".join(result)\ndef int_to_mini_roman(num: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the input integer, converts it to a Roman numeral, and returns the result in lowercase.\n    Raises ValueError for invalid input types or values outside the range [1, 1000].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if not (1 <= num <= 1000):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input integer must be between 1 and 1000.\")\n\n    converter = RomanConverter()\n    roman_upper = converter.convert(num)\n    return roman_upper.lower()"}
