{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "class DivisorCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the largest integer `d` that divides `n` evenly, where `d < n`.\n        Raises `ValueError` if `n` is not greater than 1, and `TypeError` if `n` is not an integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n <= 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be greater than 1.\")\n\n        for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return i\n        # This statement is technically unreachable for valid n > 1 as 1 is always a divisor.\n        return 1"}
