{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "from typing import List, Optional\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Identifies the longest string in a list, returning the first encountered if lengths are equal.\n    Returns `None` if the input list is empty.\n    >>> longest([])\n\n    >>> longest(['a', 'b', 'c'])\n    'a'\n    >>> longest(['a', 'bb', 'ccc'])\n    'ccc'\n    >>> longest(['apple', 'banana', 'grape'])\n    'apple'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    longest_str: Optional[str] = None\n    max_length: int = -1\n\n    for s in strings:\n        # Update longest_str if current string is longer, or if it's the very first string examined.\n        if longest_str is None or len(s) > max_length:\n            longest_str = s\n            max_length = len(s)\n    return longest_str"}
